SUMMARY:🌿🌳 SUMMER EVENING WALK: GUS HARRIS TRAIL 🌳🌿
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿🌳 SUMMER EVENING WALK: GU
 S HARRIS TRAIL 🌳🌿\n\n**A Hidden Ravine\, Easy Walking & Great Conver
 sation**\nSometimes the best parts of Toronto are the ones most people dri
 ve right past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed summer evening walk along the Gus 
 Harris Trail\, one of Toronto's hidden ravine trails that follows the peac
 eful Taylor-Massey Creek through Scarborough and East York.\n\nThis isn't 
 a challenging hike—it's an easy\, mostly flat walk that's perfect for an
 yone looking to enjoy nature\, get some fresh air\, and spend an evening w
 ith great people.\n\nThe real purpose of the walk isn't simply reaching th
 e end of the trail.\nIt's creating the space to slow down\, have conversat
 ions\, meet new people\, and enjoy a few hours away from the busyness of e
 veryday life.\n\nAlong the way we'll follow the creek\, enjoy the shade of
  the ravine\, and discover one of Toronto's quieter green spaces that many
  people never even realize exists.\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:** Taylor-Massey Cree
 k is named after two prominent Toronto families. The Taylor family owned t
 he famous Don Valley Brick Works\, now known as Evergreen Brick Works—on
 e of Toronto's most successful environmental revitalization projects.\n\n
 📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsa
 pp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\
 nWe'll spend about two hours enjoying an easy walk along the trail\, takin
 g our time\, chatting\, and getting to know one another.\n\nThis is a soci
 al walk—not a race.\n\nThere are very few hills\, making it a comfortabl
 e walk for most people with a reasonable level of fitness.\nWe'll finish b
 ack where we started before the park closes for the evening.\n\n***\n\n## 
 ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk will happen rain or shine unles
 s severe weather makes it unsafe.\nPlease wear comfortable walking shoes a
 nd dress appropriately for the weather.\n\nThe focus isn't covering as muc
 h ground as possible.\nThe focus is spending a relaxing evening outdoors w
 ith good company.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Locati
 on:** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station by Victoria Park road.\n🫎 I'
 ll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:00 PM**\nI will only
  wait **5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late.\n\n🏁 **End Sp
 ot:** Victoria Park Subway Station (before the cemetery gates close).\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 *
 *[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee
  helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events like 
 this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to B
 ring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack (optional
 )\n🌞 Bug spray or sunscreen if needed\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For
 ?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends
 —whether single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hike
 s\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's alw
 ays something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just sh
 ow up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things h
 appen and events may need to be cancelled—please keep an eye on updates.
 \n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall o
 r email:\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomovie
 sandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conv
 ersation.**\n**Leave having discovered that sometimes**\n\n**Toronto's bes
 t hidden places aren't the destination—they're simply where new friendsh
 ips begin.**
