SUMMARY:🌿🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE TRAIL EVENING WALK & PUB NIGHT 
 🍻🌿
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿🚶‍♂️ YORK BELTLINE 
 TRAIL EVENING WALK & PUB NIGHT 🍻🌿\n\n**A Hidden Urban Trail\, Easy W
 alking & A Relaxing Summer Evening**\n\nLooking for an easy way to get out
 side after work?\n\nJoin us for a summer evening walk along the York Beltl
 ine Trail\, one of Toronto's hidden green corridors.\n\nBuilt on the route
  of the historic Belt Line Railway\, this peaceful trail offers a surprisi
 ng escape from the city\, with mature trees\, birdsong\, and plenty of sha
 de—all just steps from the subway.\nThis is an easy\, mostly flat walk w
 ith no major hills\, making it perfect for anyone who wants to stretch the
 ir legs\, enjoy some fresh air\, and meet new people.\n\nAfter our walk\, 
 we'll head over to **The Bull: A Firkin Pub** for dinner and a chance to r
 elax\, chat\, and get to know one another. After all\, the walk is just th
 e beginning—the conversations afterward are where friendships often star
 t.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.
 whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll
  Do\n\nWe'll spend about **90 minutes** walking the York Beltline Trail at
  a comfortable social pace.\nAlong the way we'll enjoy one of Toronto's le
 sser-known walking trails\, share some conversation\, and unwind after the
  workday.\n\nWhen we finish\, anyone who would like to is welcome to join 
 us for dinner at **The Bull: A Firkin Pub**. You're also welcome to head h
 ome after the walk if you prefer.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectatio
 ns\n\nThis walk happens rain or shine unless severe weather makes it unsaf
 e.\nThe trail is mostly flat and suitable for most fitness levels. Please 
 wear comfortable walking shoes and bring water if it's a warm evening.\n\n
 This is a **social walk**\, not a guided historical tour. I'll share a lit
 tle history about the Beltline along the way\, but the focus is on enjoyin
 g the evening together.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup 
 Location:** Outside **Caledonia Station (North Entrance)**\n🫎 I'll be w
 earing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM**\n\nI will only wait
  **5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late.\nPlease be on time\, 
 as we will leave promptly.\n\n🏁 **End Point:** Near Davisville Station.
 \n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ After the Walk\n\nWe'll head to **The Bull: A Firkin
  Pub** for dinner and conversation.\n\n**Menu:** [Click Here!](https://www
 .firkinpubs.com/thebullandfirkin/menus/)\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n
 \n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](
 mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis fee helps support the group an
 d allows us to continue organizing events like this. Thank you for support
 ing community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Co
 mfortable walking shoes\n🍽️ Money if you'd like to join us for dinner
  afterward.\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to an
 yone who wants to be social and make friends—whether single or not.\n\nW
 e also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings
 \n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n**
 *\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're uns
 ure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to b
 e cancelled—please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:**
  Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **[torontomovie
 sandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n
 **Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n\n**Leave wonderi
 ng how one of Toronto's oldest railway lines became one of its best hidden
  walks.** 🌿🚶‍♂️🍻
