SUMMARY:🌿🚶‍♂️ NEW TRAIL! EAST DON TRAIL ADVENTURE 🍪🥾
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿🚶‍♂️ NEW! EAST DON 
 TRAIL ADVENTURE 🍪🥾\n\n**Toronto's Newest Ravine Trail\, Riverside Vi
 ews & Fresh-Baked Cookies**\n\nHave you walked Toronto's newest trail yet?
 \n\nJoin us as we explore the recently completed **East Don Trail**—one 
 of the city's newest and most exciting additions to Toronto's incredible r
 avine system. Connecting communities that were once separated\, this beaut
 iful trail follows the East Don River through peaceful forests\, wetlands\
 , and scenic valley landscapes that many Torontonians have never experienc
 ed.\n\nIf you've done the Lower Don Trail\, this is a completely different
  experience. Think quieter trails\, beautiful river views\, brand-new path
 ways\, and the feeling of discovering somewhere new.\n\nMost of the route 
 is paved and easy to walk\, making it perfect for a relaxed day outdoors.\
 nJust one warning... what goes down must come up! 😄\nThe final section 
 includes one fairly steep hill\, so while the walk is suitable for most pe
 ople\, you should be comfortable tackling a good climb at the end.\n\nAfte
 r the walk\, we'll reward ourselves with a stop at **Peak Freans Cookie Ou
 tlet**\, where you can stock up on discounted cookies and treats.\n\nThose
  who would like to continue are welcome to join us afterward for lunch at 
 **Swiss Chalet**.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join
 ](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍
 ♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll begin at Broadview Station before making our
  way into the Don Valley to explore Toronto's newest trail.\n\nAlong the w
 ay we'll:\n\n🌿 Walk beside the East Don River\n🌉 Cross new bridges a
 nd pathways\n📸 Enjoy beautiful ravine scenery\n🍪 Stop at the Peak Fr
 eans Cookie Outlet\n🍽️ Finish with an optional lunch at Swiss Chalet\
 n🚌 Return to **Coxwell Subway Station** by TTC bus.\n\nPlease note that
  **this is a one-way walk**. We will **not** return to Broadview Station.\
 n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk happens rain or sh
 ine unless severe weather makes it unsafe.\nThe trail is mostly paved and 
 relatively easy\, but there is one fairly steep hill near the end of the w
 alk.\n\nPlease come prepared for that final climb.\nThis is a social walk\
 , not a guided historical tour. We'll enjoy the scenery\, conversation\, a
 nd the chance to explore one of Toronto's newest green spaces together.\n\
 n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside **Broa
 dview Subway Station**\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat.\n⏰ **Meetup T
 ime:** **11:00 AM**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nO
 n time is late.\nPlease be on time as we will leave promptly.\n\n🏁 **En
 d Point:** Coxwell Subway Station (via TTC bus).\n\n***\n\n## 🍪 After t
 he Walk\n\nWe'll stop at the **Peak Freans Cookie Outlet**\, where you can
  browse their famous selection of cookies\, crackers\, and treats at outle
 t prices.\nAfterward\, anyone who would like to continue is welcome to joi
 n us for lunch at **Swiss Chalet**.\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$
 5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailt
 o:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allow
 s us to continue organizing events like this. Thank you for supporting com
 munity! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortab
 le walking shoes\n🍪 Spending money if you'd like cookies\n🍽️ Money
  if you'd like to join us for lunch\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\n
 This group is open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends—whe
 ther single or not.\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 
 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always some
 thing happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to just show up on
  the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen an
 d events may need to be cancelled—please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\
 n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:
 \n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandouti
 ngs@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for Toronto's newest trail.**\n**Stay for the
  cookies.**\n\n**Leave having discovered another hidden corner of the city
 's incredible ravine system.** 🌿🍪✨
